@description Rea-Sixty
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.4.4
@changelog
  - Codename: It's just a flesh wound
  - Linux: self-contained install — libusb + hidapi are now bundled next to the plugin and loaded from its own folder, so a ReaPack install works with no apt install. Fixes the "installed via ReaPack but no Control Surface / no actions" case on minimal Linux (missing libhidapi-hidraw0).
  - FX Learn: "Apply this feel to all mappings" — right-click an FX-Learn slot (or use the Learn HUD) to copy one slot's knob feel (invert / range / curve / sensitivity / polarity / push-default) onto every mapped slot in the current map. Pot controls only.
  - Sticky Pot (UF8): under FLIP the fader now follows the pinned parameter instead of the focused V-Pot param.
  - Fix: the Bindings editor shows the "Display label" field only on controls that render it (UF8 top-soft-keys), not on every button.
